        <headline>Marine Weather Statement issued September 24 at 10:25AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK</headline>
        <description>Thunderstorms continue to develop across the eastern Gulf, with
the highest activity focused along the Chichagof, Baranof and
Prince of Wales coast. While these storms are producing some
lightning, the primary threat is erratic gusty winds of 15 to 25
knots and heavy rainfall reducing visibility below 3 NM. Mariners
navigating Cape Decision to Cross Sound should be aware of this
threat and be ready for gusty winds. Thunderstorm activity should
diminish later Thursday evening.
</description>
